senses.gloss:
मरीच, अस्, m. pepper, &c., = मरिच above;
N. of a son of Kaśyapa and of a son of Sunda, (in-
correctly for मारीच, q. v.)

मारुण्ड मारुण्ड, अस्, m. a serpent's egg;
cow-dung; a place spread with cow-dung; a road,
way.

मर्कटक, अस्, m. an ape, monkey; a spider;
a kind of fish; a kind of wild panic; a species of
grain; a Daitya; (इका), f. a female ape.

मर्दित, अस्, आ, अम्, crushed, pounded, ground,
thrashed; rubbed, kneaded, squeezed; strung, tied (?);
obtained (?).

मर्यादिन्, ई, इनी, इ, having limits or boundaries;
keeping within bounds; (ई), m. a neighbour, bor-
derer.

मार्कव मार्कव, अस्, m. Eclipta Prostrata;
(sometimes incorrectly spelt मार्कर; cf. मर्-
कर.)

मार्जन, अस्, ई, अम्, wiping away, cleansing,
purifying, washing; (अस्), m. Symplocos Racemosa;
(आ), f. washing, cleansing, purifying; the sound of a
drum [cf. rt. मार्ज्]; (ई), f. a broom, besom, brush;
N. of one of Durgā's female attendants; (अम्), n.
the act of wiping or rubbing off; the act of cleaning,
scouring, cleansing, sweeping; cleansing the person
by wiping or bathing or rubbing it with unguents;
the act of wiping away or effacing; (उच्छिष्ट-
मार्जनम्, removing leavings.)

मार्त्तिकावत (fr. मृत्तिकावती), N. of a country;
epithet of the king of that country; N. of a city;
(आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; of a princely race.
